<title>USA: Dense-Pac sees &quot;significant&quot; writedown.</title>
<headline>Dense-Pac sees &quot;significant&quot; writedown.</headline>
<dateline>GARDEN GROVE, Calif. 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dense-Pac Microsystems Inc said Thursday it plans to take a significant asset write-down in the fourth quarter ending February 28 as part of its expansion of marketing, sales and research.</p>
<p>&quot;The write-down of these assets will also include severance packages, which could result in a significant one-time expense,&quot; said Chief Executive and President Uri Levy. The company did not specify the size of the expense.</p>
<p>&quot;I am very optimistic about Dense-Pac's future,&quot; Levy said.</p>
<p>The company said Levy had been elected chairman in addition to his other duties, to give him the flexibility he needs to carry out the restructuring.</p>
<p>Dense-Pac shares were up 1/16 at 2-11/16 in early trading.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsrom 212 859 1610))</p>
